args.description:
A layered-layout request: the graph, the preset its options start from, and the fields of
that preset to change.

Every part defaults, so `{}` is a valid request (an empty graph, the layered preset).

```
use graphlay::json::LayoutRequest;
use graphlay::{Direction, RoutingStyle};

let request: LayoutRequest = serde_json::from_str(r#"{
    "graph": {"nodes": [{"size": {"width": 80, "height": 40}},
                        {"size": {"width": 80, "height": 40}}],
              "edges": [{"source": 0, "target": 1}]},
    "preset": "process_map",
    "options": {"routing": {"style": "diagonal"}}
}"#)?;
let (graph, options) = request.split()?;
assert_eq!(options.routing.style, RoutingStyle::Diagonal); // from the patch
assert_eq!(options.direction, Direction::TopBottom); // from the preset
let l = graphlay::layout(&graph, &options)?;
assert!(l.nodes[0].center.y < l.nodes[1].center.y);

// A bad patch is an error that names the field.
let bad: LayoutRequest =
    serde_json::from_str(r#"{"options": {"routing": {"style": "curvy"}}}"#)?;
assert!(bad.split().unwrap_err().starts_with("options.routing.style:"));
# Ok::<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>>(())
```

parent.description:
The compound this node is drawn inside, if any. Parents must not form a cycle.
[`crate::reroute`] and [`crate::tree::layout`] reject graphs that use it.

A compound's box is its children's drawing plus [`crate::Spacing::compound_padding`] and
[`crate::Spacing::compound_header`], and at least its own [`Node::size`]. Its
[`crate::Placement`] carries that size.

```
use graphlay::{layout, GraphBuilder, LayoutOptions, Node, Rect, Size};

let mut b = GraphBuilder::new();
let order = b.add_box(Size::new(80.0, 40.0));
let billing = b.add_box(Size::new(1.0, 1.0)); // the compound, sized by its children
let inside = Node { size: Size::new(80.0, 40.0), parent: Some(billing), ..Node::default() };
let invoice = b.add_node(inside.clone());
let pay = b.add_node(inside);
b.connect(order, invoice); // crosses billing's border
b.connect(invoice, pay);
let l = layout(&b.build(), &LayoutOptions::layered_default())?;

